<title>AUSTRALIA: Bank Melbourne shares fall on bid nerves.</title>
<headline>Bank Melbourne shares fall on bid nerves.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Bank of Melbourne fell sharply on Monday morning as analysts and brokers speculated that Westpac Banking Corp may face a few political hurdles before it can complete its A$1.435 billion friendly bid.</p>
<p>Bank of Melbourne shares were 12 cents lower at A$9.35 at 11.25 a.m. (0125 GMT), a far cry from the A$9.75 high struck last Thursday's when Westpac announced the takeover.</p>
<p>Turnover in the regional bank, which specialises in home loans and small business lending, was the fourth highest on the local bourse with 1.04 million shares traded.</p>
